# Drake Hatcher's trigger is for combat damage to a player. On turn 3 Bot2's Llanowar Elves block it: Hatcher deals its
# 1 damage to the Elves (which die) and takes 1, so there is no trigger and no counter. On turn 5 Bot2 does not block and
# the 1 damage to Bot2 puts one counter on it, the positive control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Drake Hatcher
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Drake Hatcher.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Drake Hatcher)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Damage = 1
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = (absent)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = 1
